<title>UK: Scottish-Hydro sags after H1 profit dips.</title>
<headline>Scottish-Hydro sags after H1 profit dips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Scottish Hydro-Electric dipped on Thursday in meagre volume after the group reported slightly lower than expected first-half profits.</p>
<p>By 0927 GMT the stock was down 1/2p at 316-1/2p.</p>
<p>The group posted a 0.6 percent fall in first half pre-tax profits to 61.3 million sterling compared with analysts forecasts of between 63.0 and 70.7 million stg.</p>
<p>Scottish Hydro added that plans to buy out United Utilities, its 50-percent joint venture partner in Keadby power station, would raise net gearing to around 50 percent.</p>
<p>The company raised the dividend to 5.28p, from 4.75p.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
